\label{lem.FTisot}
    The action of $F_T$ on each $V(k,2\alpha+\ell)$-isotypic component of $V^{\otimes 2}$ is by the scalar $\mathrm{LG}^{(k+1)}(q^{2\alpha+\ell},q)$. Equivalently,
    \[
    F_T\circ P_{(k,\ell)}=P_{(k,\ell)}\circ F_T = \mathrm{LG}^{(k+1)}(q^{2\alpha+\ell},q)\cdot P_{(k,\ell)}
    \]

\label{lem.cisot}
    For each $V(k,2\alpha+\ell)$-isotypic component of $V^{\otimes 2}$, the braiding satisfies
    \[
    c_{k,\ell}^{2j+1}=\lambda_{k,\ell}^j c_{k,\ell} \qquad \mbox{where $\lambda_{k,\ell}=\dfrac{\theta_{V(k,2\alpha+\ell)}}{\theta_{V}^2}$.}
    \]

\label{lem.lambda}
    For $(k,\ell)$ appearing in Table \ref{table.fusion}, each of the $3n$ numbers $\lambda_{k,\ell}$ is given by the expression
    \[
    \lambda_{k,\ell}=q^{-4\alpha^2+4\alpha(n-1-k-2\ell)-2\ell(k+\ell+1)}
    \] 
    and are pairwise distinct.
